          "title": "You'll want to know: robar",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "robar — \"to steal, to rob\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Me robaron la cartera en el metro. Someone stole my wallet on the metro."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Robar algo a alguien — to steal something from someone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "robar comes from a Germanic verb raubōn 'to rob, to plunder', through Medieval Latin raubāre (EtymDB). English rob goes back to the same Germanic verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
