          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The origin of atracar is not settled. The sense 'to hold up, to mug' is often linked to the sailors' verb atracar 'to bring a boat alongside'. EtymDB traces a Spanish atracar to an Arabic verb, without saying which sense it means."
            }
          ]
        },
